export const sdkPromptSection = "# The miniapp SDK\n\nThere is nothing else: no fetch to other origins, no localStorage contract, no miniapp.db and no SQL from the browser, no miniapp.track and no analytics call: a Signal is declared on a Server Action and recorded when miniapp.actions.call runs it.\n\nBefore using an SDK module or a declaration, read its reference with read. References are available without an owner session.\n\n/reference/sdk/auth.md: Who is using the app. The Kernel owns accounts and sessions; the app only reads the current one.\nminiapp.auth.session(): Read the signed-in Runtime Actor, or the anonymous state so the app can show a sign-in button. Returns { userId, name, role }. Signed in, name is the account email and role is \"member\". Signed out, { userId: \"anonymous\", name: \"Anonymous\", role: \"anonymous\" }.\nminiapp.auth.signIn(): Send the visitor to the Deployment's login page at /_konae/login, under the page's base path. Returns nothing; the page navigates away.\nminiapp.auth.signInWithGoogle(): Send the visitor to Google through /_konae/auth/google/start. It is a navigation, so connect-src does not apply; Google returns the person to the app signed in, or to a page that says why not. Returns nothing; the page navigates away.\nminiapp.auth.signOut(): Revoke this app session and clear its cookie. Returns { ok: true }.\n\n/reference/sdk/actions.md: The only door to the database. A call names a Server Action declared in actions.json and passes its input; the Kernel authorizes the caller, binds the input and runs the action's one SQL statement, or records its Signal.\nminiapp.actions.call(name, input = {}): Invoke one declared Server Action as the current Runtime Actor. Returns an array of row objects for a query action, { changes, lastInsertId } for a mutation action, { recorded: true } for a signal action, { callId, queued: true } for a call action.\n\n/reference/sdk/page.md: Values from the page address. The Kernel fills params when a declared page path answers.\nminiapp.page.params: Read the values captured by the page path, or an empty object on a file page. Returns An object keyed by page path parameter, such as { slug: \"hello\" }.\nminiapp.page.url(path): Build an app link that keeps the current hostname or path address. Returns The path with the current /p/<name> prefix when the app uses a path address..\n\n/reference/sdk/files.md: Small files stored by the Kernel for one Deployment. The module option can require an app session to read every file.\nminiapp.files.list(): List metadata and same-origin URLs for files the current actor may read. Returns an array of { id, name, type, size, visibility, createdAt, ownerId, url }. ownerId is present only on files the caller uploaded. url is the path files.url returns for the file. The Kernel serves JavaScript, HTML, XML and SVG types as application/octet-stream.\nminiapp.files.upload(file, options): Store a File or Blob for the signed-in user and return it as files.list would. Returns { id, name, type, size, visibility, createdAt, ownerId, url }, where url is the path files.url returns for the new file.\nminiapp.files.url(fileId): The address of a stored file on the app's own origin, for an img src, a link or a fetch. Returns a Promise of the path \"<base>/_konae/files/<id>\", where <base> is the page's base path: empty, or /p/<id-or-name> on a path address. Reading it answers the file's bytes with its own type when the caller may read it, 404 File not found when the file is missing, deleted or access is denied, and 401 authentication-required to a visitor of a private Deployment.\nminiapp.files.update(fileId, { visibility }): Make a file the signed-in user uploaded public or private. Publishing a draft keeps its ID, so no second copy counts against the quota. Returns { id, name, type, size, visibility, createdAt, ownerId } with the new visibility. There is no url; the ID and its files.url path stay the same.\nminiapp.files.delete(fileId): Delete a file the signed-in user uploaded. Its bytes are gone and its size stops counting against the Deployment's quota. Returns { id, deleted: true }.\n\n/reference/sdk/calls.md: Calls from this app to another app or an outside service, made by the Kernel from its own process, never from the browser. There is no browser call: the page invokes the call action with miniapp.actions.call, which answers { callId, queued: true }, and the Kernel sends the request, retries it and runs the then mutation with the answer.\n\n/reference/sdk/http.md: Routes on the Deployment's own host for programs and other services: a JSON endpoint, a webhook, a file a program fetches. There is no browser call; the app's own pages keep using miniapp.actions.call, and may use a file's route as an img src.\n\n/reference/sdk/seo.md: Canonical addresses and page cards for HTML pages, robots.txt and a sitemap when the owner turns search listing on.\n\n/reference/sdk/functions.md: Run bundled JavaScript handlers on the Kernel with verified identity and named Server Actions.";

